fio: fio (a flexible I/O tester)
fio:
fio: Fio spawns a number of threads or processes doing a particular type 
fio: of I/O action as specified by the user. fio takes a number of global
fio: parameters, each inherited by the thread unless otherwise parameters
fio: given to them overriding that setting is given. The typical use of 
fio: fio is to write a job file matching the I/O load one wants to 
fio: simulate.
